# One production-size stage-1 task: 20,000 synthetic stars against 4,087 synthetic clusters ("about 20,000 stars per
# task", AGENTS.md), the same stars as screen.wu and 18,000 more. Use it for the final number of a change that screen.wu
# shows, and for the GPU apps: the CUDA/OpenCL app did 20,000 stars in about 12 s on an RTX 5070 Ti (commit 8bb46cb), so
# only a task this size makes the GPU part longer than the one-time cluster precompute on the host.
# Header as in screen.wu.
# Expected on an Apple M1, CPU app: about 7 minutes (20,000 x 0.02 s plus the precompute); a GPU host: well under a
# minute. Expected, not measured. Three rounds of two builds take about 45 minutes on the M1.
header PHYGAS 1 screen 25 64 2 0.001
clusters 4087
targets 20000
kind S
seed 1
